// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > 531 1`] = `
"4 sessions a week · four different days
Repeats in 4-week cycles: 5s week, 3s week, 5/3/1 week and Deload.
After each cycle, raise your training max: +5 lb on Overhead Press and Bench Press and +10 lb on Back Squat and Deadlift.
Percentages are of your training max for each lift.

Day 1 · Press: MAIN OHP · SUPP OHP
Day 2 · Deadlift: MAIN DEADLIFT · SUPP DEADLIFT
Day 3 · Bench: MAIN BENCH · SUPP BENCH
Day 4 · Squat: MAIN SQUAT · SUPP SQUAT

[Main · % of training max] (Overhead Press, Deadlift, Bench Press, Back Squat)
5s week: 5 @ 65%, 5 @ 75%, 5+ @ 85%. 3s week: 3 @ 70%, 3 @ 80%, 3+ @ 90%. 5/3/1 week: 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 85%, 1+ @ 95%. Deload: 5 @ 40%, 5 @ 50%, 5 @ 60%.
[Supplemental · % of training max] (Overhead Press, Deadlift, Bench Press, Back Squat)
Every week: 5×10 @ 50%. Skipped on deload weeks."
`;

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > gzclp 1`] = `
"4 sessions a week · four different days
Open-ended: keep running it as long as you progress.

Day A1 · Squat: T1 SQUAT · T2 BENCH · T3 LAT PD
Day B1 · OHP: T1 OHP · T2 DEADLIFT · T3 DB ROW
Day A2 · Bench: T1 BENCH · T2 SQUAT · T3 LAT PD
Day B2 · Deadlift: T1 DEADLIFT · T2 OHP · T3 DB ROW

[T1 · 5×3+ → 6×2+ → 10×1+] (Back Squat, Overhead Press, Bench Press, Deadlift)
5×3+ (last set as many reps as you can). Get every rep and add 10 lb on Back Squat and Deadlift and 5 lb on Overhead Press and Bench Press next time. If you miss a rep, move to 6×2+, then 10×1+ at the same weight. When 10×1+ stalls too, test a new 5-rep max and restart at 85% of it.
[T2 · 3×10 → 3×8 → 3×6] (Bench Press, Deadlift, Back Squat, Overhead Press)
3×10. Get every rep and add 5 lb on Bench Press and Overhead Press and 10 lb on Deadlift and Back Squat next time. If you miss a rep, move to 3×8, then 3×6 at the same weight. When 3×6 stalls too, go back to 3×10 at the weight you last did it with, plus 10 lb on Bench Press and Overhead Press and 20 lb on Deadlift and Back Squat.
[T3 · 3×15+] (Lat Pulldown, Dumbbell Row)
3×15+. When the first two sets get 15 and the last set reaches 25 reps, add 5 lb next time; until then, keep the weight and push the last set."
`;

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > nsuns5 1`] = `
"5 sessions a week · five different days
Open-ended: keep running it as long as you progress.
Percentages are of your training max for each lift.

Day 1 · Bench volume / OHP: T1 BENCH · T2 OHP
Day 2 · Squat / Sumo: T1 SQUAT · T2 SUMO DL
Day 3 · OHP / Incline: T1 OHP · T2 INCLINE
Day 4 · Deadlift / Front squat: T1 DEADLIFT · T2 FRONT SQ
Day 5 · Bench / CG bench: T1 BENCH · T2 CG BENCH

[T1 · % of training max · Day 1 · Bench volume / OHP] (Bench Press)
Bench Press (Day 1 · Bench volume / OHP): 8 @ 65%, 6 @ 75%, 3×4 @ 85%, 5 @ 80%, 6 @ 75%, 7 @ 70%, 8+ @ 65%.
[T1 · % of training max] (Back Squat, Deadlift)
Back Squat (Day 2 · Squat / Sumo): 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 85%, 1+ @ 95%, 3 @ 90%, 3 @ 85%, 3 @ 80%, 5 @ 75%, 5 @ 70%, 5+ @ 65%. Deadlift (Day 4 · Deadlift / Front squat): 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 85%, 1+ @ 95%, 3 @ 90%, 3 @ 85%, 3 @ 80%, 3 @ 75%, 3 @ 70%, 3+ @ 65%. Reps on the 1+ set move your training max: 0–1 reps: no change · 2–3 reps: +5 lb · 4–5 reps: +10 lb · 6+ reps: +15 lb. The change applies from the next week.
[T1 · % of training max] (Overhead Press, Bench Press)
Overhead Press (Day 3 · OHP / Incline): 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 85%, 1+ @ 95%, 3 @ 90%, 3 @ 85%, 3 @ 80%, 5 @ 75%, 5 @ 70%, 5+ @ 65%. Bench Press (Day 5 · Bench / CG bench): 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 85%, 1+ @ 95%, 3 @ 90%, 5 @ 85%, 3 @ 80%, 5 @ 75%, 3 @ 70%, 5+ @ 65%. Reps on the 1+ set move your training max: 0–1 reps: no change · 2–5 reps: +5 lb · 6+ reps: +10 lb. The change applies from the next week.
[T2 · % of training max] (Overhead Press, Sumo Deadlift, Incline Bench Press, Close-Grip Bench, Front Squat)
Overhead Press (Day 1 · Bench volume / OHP): 6 @ 50%, 5 @ 60%, 3 @ 70%, 5 @ 70%, 7 @ 70%, 4 @ 70%, 6 @ 70%, 8 @ 70%. Sumo Deadlift (Day 2 · Squat / Sumo): 5 @ 50%, 5 @ 60%, 3 @ 70%, 5 @ 70%, 7 @ 70%, 4 @ 70%, 6 @ 70%, 8 @ 70%. Incline Bench Press and Close-Grip Bench: 6 @ 40%, 5 @ 50%, 3 @ 60%, 5 @ 60%, 7 @ 60%, 4 @ 60%, 6 @ 60%, 8 @ 60%. Front Squat (Day 4 · Deadlift / Front squat): 5 @ 35%, 5 @ 45%, 3 @ 55%, 5 @ 55%, 7 @ 55%, 4 @ 55%, 6 @ 55%, 8 @ 55%. Variations are loaded off their parent lift's training max."
`;

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > sbsRtf 1`] = `
"4 sessions a week · different sessions each week
A 21-week block that ends after week 21.
Percentages are of your max for each lift.

Day 1 · Squat (weeks 1–6, 8–13 and 15–20): MAIN SQUAT · SUPP INCLINE · SUPP SUMO DL
Deload Day 1 · Squat (weeks 7, 14 and 21): MAIN SQUAT · SUPP INCLINE · SUPP SUMO DL
Day 2 · Bench (weeks 1–6, 8–13 and 15–20): MAIN BENCH · SUPP FRONT SQ · SUPP PUSH PRESS
Deload Day 2 · Bench (weeks 7, 14 and 21): MAIN BENCH · SUPP FRONT SQ · SUPP PUSH PRESS
Day 3 · Deadlift (weeks 1–6, 8–13 and 15–20): MAIN DEADLIFT · SUPP CG BENCH
Deload Day 3 · Deadlift (weeks 7, 14 and 21): MAIN DEADLIFT · SUPP CG BENCH
Day 4 · OHP (weeks 1–6, 8–13 and 15–20): MAIN OHP · SUPP PAUSE SQ
Deload Day 4 · OHP (weeks 7, 14 and 21): MAIN OHP · SUPP PAUSE SQ

[Main · % of max] (Back Squat, Bench Press, Deadlift, Overhead Press)
Changes every week over 21 weeks: sets of 1–10 reps at 70–95%, with AMRAP sets. The WORKOUTS tab lists each week. The last (AMRAP) set has a rep target, and beating or missing it moves your max: 2+ short: −5% · 1 short: −2% · on target: no change · 1 over: +0.5% · 2 over: +1% · 3 over: +1.5% · 4 over: +2% · 5+ over: +3%. Skipping a planned set at that weight, or coming up short on one, counts as 2+ short.
[Main · % of max] (Back Squat, Bench Press, Deadlift, Overhead Press)
Weeks 7, 14 and 21: 5×5 @ 60%.
[Supplemental · % of max] (Incline Bench Press, Sumo Deadlift, Front Squat, Push Press, Close-Grip Bench, Pause Squat)
Changes every week over 21 weeks: sets of 2–14 reps at 60–85%, with AMRAP sets. The WORKOUTS tab lists each week. The last (AMRAP) set has a rep target, and beating or missing it moves your max: 2+ short: −5% · 1 short: −2% · on target: no change · 1 over: +0.5% · 2 over: +1% · 3 over: +1.5% · 4 over: +2% · 5+ over: +3%. Skipping a planned set at that weight, or coming up short on one, counts as 2+ short.
[Supplemental · % of max] (Incline Bench Press, Sumo Deadlift, Front Squat, Push Press, Close-Grip Bench, Pause Squat)
Weeks 7, 14 and 21: 5×5 @ 50%."
`;

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > smolov-jr 1`] = `
"4 sessions a week · four different days
A 3-week block that ends after week 3.
Percentages are of your 1RM for each lift.

Day 1 · 6×6 @ 70%: MAIN SQUAT
Day 2 · 7×5 @ 75%: MAIN SQUAT
Day 3 · 8×4 @ 80%: MAIN SQUAT
Day 4 · 10×3 @ 85%: MAIN SQUAT

[Main · % of 1RM · Day 1 · 6×6 @ 70%] (Back Squat)
Week 1: 6×6 @ 70%. Then every set gets heavier: +10 lb in week 2 and +20 lb in week 3. Your 1RM stays the same throughout.
[Main · % of 1RM · Day 2 · 7×5 @ 75%] (Back Squat)
Week 1: 7×5 @ 75%. Then every set gets heavier: +10 lb in week 2 and +20 lb in week 3. Your 1RM stays the same throughout.
[Main · % of 1RM · Day 3 · 8×4 @ 80%] (Back Squat)
Week 1: 8×4 @ 80%. Then every set gets heavier: +10 lb in week 2 and +20 lb in week 3. Your 1RM stays the same throughout.
[Main · % of 1RM · Day 4 · 10×3 @ 85%] (Back Squat)
Week 1: 10×3 @ 85%. Then every set gets heavier: +10 lb in week 2 and +20 lb in week 3. Your 1RM stays the same throughout."
`;

exports[`describeProgram > snapshots > stronglifts 1`] = `
"3 sessions a week · two days that alternate, so the order shifts week to week
Open-ended: keep running it as long as you progress.

Workout A · Squat / Bench / Row: MAIN SQUAT · MAIN BENCH · MAIN BB ROW
Workout B · Squat / OHP / Deadlift: MAIN SQUAT · MAIN OHP · MAIN DEADLIFT

[Main · 5×5] (Back Squat, Bench Press, Barbell Row, Overhead Press)
5×5. Get every rep and add 5 lb next time. If you miss reps three sessions in a row, drop the weight 10% and build back up.
[Main · 1×5] (Deadlift)
1×5. Get every rep and add 10 lb next time. If you miss reps three sessions in a row, drop the weight 10% and build back up."
`;
